<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Modest Mussorgsky</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1839">1839</a>–<a href="/years/1881">1881</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Mussorgsky</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Modest Mussorgsky was a nineteenth-century Russian composer, known for works such as the opera <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boris-godunov">Boris Godunov</a> and Pictures at an Exhibition. He belonged to a group of composers who sought a distinctively Russian national music. He is among the cultural figures of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/modest-mussorgsky.jpg" alt="Modest Mussorgsky" width="320" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Modest_Musorgskiy,_1870.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
